# Git push
When the user says "push update" (or similar): stage and commit all relevant changes. The agent cannot run `git push` (no GitHub credentials in this environment). After committing, reply in one line that they should run `git push` locally—do not repeat long explanations.

# Links and navigation (CRITICAL — has caused many hours of rework)
- **Nav/dropdown links:** Use plain `<a href="...">`, not Next.js `<Link>`, so clicks actually navigate. Same pattern as the Blue Program link in the navbar. Radix dropdown + Link often blocks navigation.
- **Before saying any nav or "we're good":** (1) Confirm every menu item has a real route (file exists for that path). (2) Use the same link pattern as existing working items (e.g. Blue, Rankings). (3) Do not assume links work; check how working links are implemented in this codebase first.
- **New pages:** If adding a nav item, create the route first, then add the link using the working pattern.
